<title>JAPAN: Table of party strengths in Japan's parliament.</title>
<headline>Table of party strengths in Japan's parliament.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Here is a table of party strengths in the two houses of Japan's parliament. The Liberal Democratic Party (LDP), whose leader Ryutaro Hashimoto was re-elected prime minister on Thursday, has formed a loose alliance with the Social Democrats and the Sakigake party:</p>
<p> Party..............Lower House.........Upper House</p>
<p> LDP................239......................110</p>
<p> Social Democrats....15.......................33</p>
<p> Sakigake.............2........................3</p>
<p>-----------------------------------------------</p>
<p> Shinshinto.........153.......................68</p>
<p> Democrats...........52........................5</p>
<p> Communists..........26.......................14</p>
<p> Minor/Independents..13.......................18</p>
<p> Vacant...............0........................1</p>
<p>===============================================</p>
<p> Total..............500......................252</p>
</text>
